<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Tuesday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p>B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p>C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p>E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p>F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p>G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p>H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>   Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*  *G*   *H*</p>
<p>Jun 17  21,811 5,319 27,130 13,808 13,841 6,388  0  20,229</p>
<p>Jun 18  21.576 5,435 27,011 13,659 13,689 6,376  0  20.065</p>
<p>Jun 19  21,556 5,300 26,856 13,590 13,621 6,441  0  20,062</p>
<p>Jun 20  21,578 5,448 27,026 13,562 13,593 6,490  0  20,083</p>
<p>Jun 23  21,353 5,378 26,731 13,556 13,590 6,256  0  19,846</p>
<p>Jun 24  21,021 5,333 26,354 13,484 13,515 5,999  0  19,514</p>
<p>Jun 25  21,262 5,297 26,559 13,485 13,491 6,260  0  19,751</p>
<p>Jun 26  21,259 5,469 26,728 13,609 13,613 6,140  0  19,753</p>
<p>Jun 27  21,410 5,606 27,016 13,809 13,814 6,069  0  19,883</p>
<p>*A  Of the $21.41 billion in international reserves, $1.84 billion (8.59 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0651))</p>
